# iCloud Drive conflict copies. ~/Documents is synced by iCloud when
# "Desktop & Documents Folders" is on, and the bird daemon creates
# "<name> 2.<ext>" copies when a build writes many files at once. javac and
# Flyway both pick these up from the source tree and fail: duplicate classes,
# and two migrations claiming the same version. Ignoring them stops them being
# committed, but the real fix is to move the repo off a synced folder.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9][0-9].*
